{"name":"Underwater World","hex":"#657f7a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"underwater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Beneath the surface of the water; of or pertaining to the region beneath the water surface.","Beneath the water line of a vessel."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["So as to go beneath the surface of the water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underwater"},{"term":"world","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The subjective human experience, regarded collectively; human collective existence; existence in general; the reality we live in.","The subjective human experience, regarded individually."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider or cause to be considered from a global perspective; to consider as a global whole, rather than making or focusing on national or other distinctions; compare globalize.","To make real; to make worldly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/world"}],"entries":[{"title":"Underwater World, Singapore","blocks":[{"text":"Underwater World, also known as Underwater World Singapore Pte Ltd, was an oceanarium located on the offshore Singaporean island of Sentosa. It was opened on 13 May 1991 and closed on 26 June 2016."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/61/Underwater_World_Singapore_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwater_World%2C_Singapore","wikidata":"Q2125883"},{"title":"Underwater World (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Underwater World\" is single released in 1984 by the Finnish rock and glam punk band Hanoi Rocks. \"Underwater World\" is from the band's US-breakthrough album Two Steps From The Move, and was released as a single and as an EP in August 1984 in Finland and in November in the UK."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/UnderwaterWorldSingle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_co